Z||000000||Philphine||10-28-2000||11:19 PM||||<BR>no i don't own 120 pairs of skimpy undewear.<P>got a 120 mph speedo cluster. can i put it in my '87 4cyl coupe with out mods? i actually got it in hope that i would need it for an eventual engine swap (picking up the little things as i go and/or find them). would it be plug and play for now or is more needed? i know i'll lose my oil pressure guage but will use an aftermarket one.<P>maybe better to box it up till i know i'm doing an engine change?||||reg||1
Z||000001||robertjay||10-29-2000||12:40 AM||||I asked the same ? to he Fiero Store, and this was their response:<P>Robert,<P>Pull the old speedo out and plug in the 120 speedo.  Very easy, just need to<BR>find the 120mph speedo.<P>Thanks<BR>The Fiero Store<P><BR>So sounds like it just Plug-And-Play, I haven't personally tried it yet, but hopefully they are a reliable source.  Later!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-29-2000||07:17 AM||||The 120mph speedo is backlit.  Are your current gauges backlit, too?  I know the '86 and up GTs and SEs were, but the 4 cyls?  If not, your dash will look funny at least.  At worst, it will be incompatible as the "bezel plate" (no idea what the correct term is) will be different.||||reg||1
